Town phase 2 done (claude/town-phase2, from origin/main ce78c043). PR title and body: .pr-body.md. No PR opened, so CI has not run (it
runs on a PR): please open it with the `full-e2e` label (it changes the town's loading screen). One branch, nothing split off. About
5 hours, over the 4 the brief names: the last hour went on two things the first e2e run found (below), not on new scope.

What it does (the brief's five points)
1. The picture service (town/picture-service.ts): tags, home names, bubbles and their tail, signs, the clock, table pieces, the zzz,
   pawns, outfits and rides, the sky, the statues' close-ups and quotes are asked for by key (`svc.ask`), made and uploaded in a
   slice after each draw (3 ms, feel.ts `picSliceMs`; under the loading card until nothing waits), drawn when ready, left out until
   then. paint-gl.ts `entry` no longer uploads: that call is gone, with the painter's own text and shadowed-fill canvases, `changed`,
   the sweep and the page reset. A picture that didn't come through the door isn't drawn. 1c's leftovers are ended too: `planBoxes`
   paints nothing ahead, `FrameCache.get`, `roofArt` and the glows only look up, and a roof that isn't baked fails the load.
2. Text at one size: the stills went up first (stills/town-phase2, 5 images and a README; `.mockup` on this branch). My reading, and
   what's built: one picture a name scaled by the GPU from a pixel ratio of 1.5 (every phone, a 2x laptop: it can't be told apart);
   on a 1x screen a picture for every size, as before. Not "two sizes": at 1x the smallest tags went dim scaled (e2e/town-tags.spec.ts's
   own check failed on the computer: a sidekick's pill's fully white pixels, 3% → 0.6%), and two sizes didn't help (9 scaled to 8 is as
   soft as 12 scaled to 8). One line to change: feel.ts `picOneSizeFrom` (0: one size everywhere); `tagPicSizes`, `namePicSizes`.
   This is my call, not the director's answer: nothing came back before I had to go on.
3. Bubbles ahead of their line: each boss's next line is picked ahead (world.ts `bossNextLine`), its bubble asked for while the boss is
   on screen, and a boss talks only once it's made (`lineReady`). The goodbye line's bubble is made on the loading screen.
4. Tags never overflow: the text has atlas pages of its own (2 on a phone), a freed place is the next picture's, a full group lets go
   what was drawn least lately (never one drawn in this frame or the last). The reset code is deleted, not guarded.
5. Measured, same machine, main's build then this one (headless Chromium, software WebGL, phone slowed 4x)
   - Busy walk, 55 players and 12 seated: uploads inside frames 143 → 0; pages started again 1 → 0. Half wearing, second walk:
     152 → 0 and 1 → 0. Between frames on the walks: the two statues' close-ups (about 30 ms in all), nothing else.
   - Our parts a frame: busy 16.2 → 14.9 ms; the empty town 20.0 → 13.5 (the close-ups were built inside frames). Budget held
     (busy under 1.25 of empty).
   - Text 8.67 M pixels → 1.29 M (with the 67 players' tags: 3.61 M, on its 2 pages). Atlas 15 pages → 14 (a 1x computer: 13 → 14).
   - Load, in reference jobs: main 5.6 to 7.1, this 4.2 to 5.0 (budget 8; this machine was noisier than in 1c's runs).
   - Same pixels: a player's town n 2250, hash 81fb216, gpu 8f62dba3 (main's, 1c's).

Found by the first e2e run, fixed
- I had the slice wait for the browser to be idle. A busy device never is: a ride took about half a minute to appear (e2e "rides
  lazy" failed). It runs after every draw now, in its own task.
- A statue's quote size was read from its picture, which now arrives a frame or two later: it's read from the layout.

Not verified, for the director
- CI. Locally green: typecheck; the app's town unit tests (435); e2e town-street, town-tags, town, town-fixed, town-rows,
  town-controls, town-desktop, town-afk, town-ranked, town-leave, boss-challenge, town-chat on both projects (188 passed) at ab51ab70;
  after that the freed-places refactor, the pixel-ratio test and its counter went in, and I re-ran only the changed and nearby tests
  (the pixel ratio's 3 times, the roam, both lost-context tests, the bubble, rides lazy, tags) and the 5 @perf town tests. Not run
  locally: the rest of the suite (the area's other traced specs: boss-character, boss-smoke, colosseum, front-door, lobby-chat, shop,
  town-chat-history).
- Real GPUs and iOS Safari: a freed place taken again is cleared with a zero upload first (texSubImage3D from a typed array), new in
  this phase and run only on software WebGL here. Worth a `/town?report` on Eric's phone and laptop: its line now says
  "Between frames: N made, M uploaded (X ms)".
- One step of a statue's close-up is 16 to 30 ms on the slowed phone (one layer drawn), now in a task between frames where it was
  inside one. Unchanged work, better placed, but still a long task.

Left, not done
- 1c's review nit "a lost context in a room can end the visit": not touched (it's the restore's failure path, not this phase's).
- Looks have no cap beyond their pages' room (2 or 3 pages): past it a newcomer stays plain or on foot until someone's look, not drawn
  for a while, makes room. Before, the spare pages thrashed. Fifty-five different rides at once would show it.
- The rooms (ShopRoom) and the Colosseum draw with their own code: untouched.

Changed checks, old → new: in .pr-body.md. No check that guards a rule in docs/rules/eric.md changed. Stills: branch
stills/town-phase2. Local e2e needed its own Playwright config for this container's browser build: not committed.
